  "raw_text": "144\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nbh11\n):\n \nDia ba pain sapa, dia ba saura sapa witin uba aman lukisa\n \n–\n \nHe cares deeply about what is right and what is\n\nwrong\n \n/ Se preocupa profundamente por lo que está bien y lo que está mal)\n\nAman luki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto examine carefully, to consider carefully, to carefully analyze, to meditate\n \n/\n\nexaminar cuidadosamente, considerar cuidadosamente, analizar cuidadosamente, meditar\n\nSelp aman lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto\n \nconsider oneself carefully, to analyze oneself\n \n/ considerarse cuidadosamente,\n\nanalizarse\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nbh94\n):\n \nYawan kumi bani selp aman lukaia sa\n \n–\n \nWe all must analyze ourselves\n \n/ Todos debemos analizarnos\n\na nosotros mismos)\n\nDiara sut ba saura takbia\n \nlukaia\n \n(\nfy16\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think all things will be bad, to think negatively\n \n/ pensar que todas\n\nlas cosas serán\n \nmalas, pensar negativamente\n\nKasak lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto believe, to have faith, to have confidence, to trust\n \n/ creer, tener fe, tener confianza, confiar\n\nKasak lukan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nKasak lukanka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nfaith\n \n/ fe\n\n(Construct:\n \nKasakki lukan lâka\n \n–\n \nmy faith\n \n/ mi fe;\n \nKasakkam lukan lâka\n \n–\n \nyour faith\n \n/ tu fe;\n \nAi kasakka lukan lâka\n\n(a/t:\n \nAi kasak lukan lâka)\n \n–\n \nhis/her faith\n \n/ su fe)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndbta-Jems 2:26\n):\n \nKasak lukan lâka (ba) daukanka yamni...marikras kaka, ... pruan sa\n \n–\n \nFaith without\nshowing good deeds is dead.\n/ La fe sin mostrar buenas obras está muerta.\n \nNote/Nota:\n \ndb,dba\n \nuse\n \nmaikras\n\ninstead of\n \nmarikras\n \nwhich appears to be a mistake.\n \nbh55\n \nquotes\n \ndbta\n \nwhich is correct\n.\n \n/\n \ndb,dba\n \nusa\n \nmaikras\n \nen\n\nlugar de\n \nmarikras\n, lo que parece ser un error.\n \nbh55\n \ncita\n \ndbta\n \nque es correcto.\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh104\n):\n \nNahki wan kasak lukan lâka ba kau karna daukisa?\n \n–\n \nHow can we make our faith more strong?\n \n/\n¿Cómo podemos fortalecer nuestra fe?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n):\n \nKasakkam lukan lâka dukiara aisas\n \n–\n \nExplain your beliefs\n \n/ Explique sus creencias)\n\nKasak lukan lâka karna daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto strengthen faith\n \n/ para fortalecer la fe\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-08/20\n):\n \nAni Baibil sturka ba hilp wan munaia sip sa wan kasakka lukan lâka karna daukaia ?\n\n–\n \nWhich Bible account can help us strengthen our faith?\n \n/ ¿Qué relato bíblico puede ayudarnos a\nfortalecer nuestra fe?)\n\nKasak lalukra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nfaithful person\n \n/ persona fiel\n\nKasak lukan lâka marikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto show faith\n \n/ mostrar fe\n\nRait kasakka lukan lâka\n \n–\n \ntrue faith, real faith\n \n/ verdadera fe\n\nKasak lukras\n \n–\n \nnot having faith, not showing faith, not believing, not trusting\n \n/ no tener fe, no mostrar fe,\nno creer, no confiar\n\nKunin lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto doubt, to believe something is not true\n \n/ dudar, creer que algo no es verdad\n\nKupia lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think, to consider, to care\n \n/ pensar, considerar,\n \npreocuparse,\n \ninteresar\nse por bien estar de\n\nalguien\n\nKupia lukanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthinking, mind, ability to think, thought\n \n/ pensamiento, mente, capacidad de\npensar\n\nKupia lukra\n \n–\n \nthought, thoughts, thinking, thoughts of the heart, caring thought(s), idea\n \n/ pensamiento,\npensamientos, pensamientos del corazón, pensamiento(s) considerado(s), idea\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfy148\n):\n \nBaibil t\nâ\nnka kasak ba upla kupia lukra ba chens munisa\n \n–\n \nA\nccurate Bible knowledge changes\n\npeople’s thinking\n \n/ El conocimiento exacto de la Biblia cambia el pensamiento de las personas\n)\n\nKupia lukra kuninkira\n \n(\ndb\n-\nJirimaya 17:9\n)\n \n–\n \ndeceivous thoughts, treacherous thoughts\n \n/\n\npensamientos engañosos, pensamientos traicioneros\n\nKupia lukras\n \n–\n \nnot think, not care\n \n/ no pensar, no importar\n\nKupi lukras\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nI don’t care\n \n/ no me importa;\n \nKupiam lukras\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nyou don’t care\n \n/ no te\nimporta\n\nLalukra\n \n(see/ver:\n \nLukaia\n) (adj,n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nthinker, thoughtful, one who is thoughtful, one who thinks, one\nwho is faithful, faithful believer\n \n/ pensador, reflexivo, uno que es reflexivo, uno que piensa, uno que es fiel, fiel\ncreyente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/21\n):\n \nupla lalukra kum wal baman marit takaia\n \n–\n \nto get married only with a believer\n \n(“only in the Lord”\n-\nnwt-\n1Kor7:39\n)\n \n/ casarse solo con un/una creyente (“solo en el Se\nñ\nor”\n-\ntnm-1Kor7:39\n))\n\nKasak lalukra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nfaithful person\n \n/ persona fiel\n\nUpla lalukra apia\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nnon-\nbeliever, person who doesn’t think\n \n/ no creyente, persona que\nno piensa\n\nLukaia sip tanka ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthinking ability, the ability to think\n \n/ capacidad de pensar",
